<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vyachko</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1224</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Vyachko of Koknese, Vyacheslav Borisovich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vyachko was a Rus' prince of the Polotsk dynasty who ruled Koknese on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-dvina">Daugava</a> in present-day Latvia. Pressed by the Livonian crusaders, he ceded half his land to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-of-riga">Albert of Riga</a> in 1207, then burned Koknese and withdrew in 1208. Later given <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tartu">Tartu</a> by Novgorod, he defended it against the crusaders and was killed when it fell in 1224.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vyachko.jpg" alt="Vyachko" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tapazi · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vyachko.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
